<title>UK: Safeway recruits to reduce Christmas queues.</title>
<headline>Safeway recruits to reduce Christmas queues.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>British supermarket chain Safeway Plc said it planned to cut queues for shoppers over the Christmas period by creating the equivalent of 500 full-time jobs at a cost of two million stg in a &quot;Queue Busters&quot; campaign.</p>
<p>In a statement, the store group said the Queue Busters would pack bags and serve behind checkouts, speciality counters, coffee shops and kiosks.</p>
<p>The group said the initiative would be &quot;on-going,&quot; not only over the busy Christmas period.</p>
<p>Safeway said Queue Busters had already been trialled in six stores for over a year and &quot;queue times and overall customer perception of Safeway's customer services standards (were) significantly improved.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
